# Dashboard layout (do not break)

The sidebar shell lives in **[`terrana-dashboard-shell.css`](src/styles/terrana-dashboard-shell.css)** (imported after `globals.css` in root [`layout.tsx`](src/app/layout.tsx)) and **[`dashboard-shell.tsx`](src/components/layout/dashboard-shell.tsx)** (markup only).

## Rules

1. **Never** put viewport height, grid columns, or sidebar visibility in Tailwind classes on the shell — use `data-layout` + `terrana-dashboard-shell.css`.
2. **Never** duplicate dashboard layout rules in `globals.css` — one file only.
3. **Never** return a React fragment with multiple layout roots from sidebar components.
4. Nav content only in `app-sidebar.tsx` — use `[data-layout="sidebar-inner"]` and `[data-layout="sidebar-nav-scroll"]`.
5. Root [`layout.tsx`](src/app/layout.tsx) uses `data-terrana-app` on `<html>` — not Tailwind `h-svh` / `overflow-hidden`.
6. Sidebar nav links use `data-nav-link` + [`terrana-sidebar-nav.css`](src/styles/terrana-sidebar-nav.css) — not Tailwind flex/padding on links.
7. Main content scrolls in `<main data-layout="dashboard-page-scroll">` — not the document body.
8. Critical layout properties use `!important` in shell/nav CSS so HMR / utility classes cannot override.

## Verify after any layout change

Run `npm run test:layout` (also in `npm run test:health`).

Manual checks:

- Super admin + accounts on desktop: dark sidebar full viewport height, sign out pinned bottom
- Long list page: only white main area scrolls, sidebar stays fixed
- Mobile: hamburger menu visible, no desktop sidebar strip
